WEBVTT

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.740
Everyone, Kaleido Star is about to start.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.440
When you watch Kaleido Star,
please keep your room bright,

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.100
and sit as far from the TV as you can.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.520
Well, well, well. Do you know
someone among your friends

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.580
who likes to make everybody laugh?

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.480
Anna told me that her father used to
make her laugh a lot when she was little.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:21.890
But the father she met after not seeing
him for a long time,

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.220
is completely different.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.130
When something like this happens,
I wonder if there is anything I can do.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.600
I wonder. I wonder.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.640
<i>What is it that you want to do?</i>

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.640
<i>Yaritai koto wa nani</i>

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.310
<i>Every time I was asked that</i>

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.310
<i>Sou kikareru tabi</i>

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:53.040
<i>I looked up at the blue sky</i>

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:53.040
<i>Aoi sora miageta</i>

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.060
<i>The answer is only in my heart</i>

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.060
<i>Kotae wa only my heart</i>

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:04.570
<i>I don't easily say the words
that are really important</i>

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:04.570
<i>Honto ni daiji na kotoba wa
kantan ni wa iwanai</i>

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:11.870
<i>I start running towards the place
the light points to</i>

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:11.870
<i>Hikari ga yubisasu basho e to hashiridasu yo</i>

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:19.820
<i>There's so much in my heart that I want
to embrace, I could cry</i>

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:19.820
<i>Dakishimetai mono nara
nakitai hodo mune ni aru</i>

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:26.790
<i>I'll keep painting my way, I promise,
take it someday</i>

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:26.790
<i>Egakitsuzukete yuku kitto
take it someday</i>

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:34.760
<i>Beyond the horizon, where the white
clouds drift</i>

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:34.760
<i>Shiroi kumo ga nagareru
chiheisen no mukou ni</i>

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:46.500
<i>The future is lined up and
it'll always be there by my side</i>

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:46.500
<i>Naranderu mirai wa itsumo soba ni aru kara</i>

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.400
Anna, you're the best!

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:30.190
Anna's Not So Amazing Father

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:31.020
Anna's Not So Amazing Father

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:31.020
"Anna's

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.020
Anna's Not So Amazing Father

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.020
Not So Amazing

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:32.990
Anna's Not So Amazing Father

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:32.990
Father"

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:35.890
Anna's Not So Amazing Father

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:42.360
It seems your fans are coming
to see you everyday, Anna.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:46.390
Anna, I think you should be a little more
sociable with your fans.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:48.900
Like this?

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.960
Not good?

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:53.540
Unfortunately...

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.930
Your fans will cry if they see you like that.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.100
Ouch!

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:01.040
I think I still have a long way to go.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.950
Hey, Anna, why did you join Kaleido Stage?

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.010
I know you like to make people laugh.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.760
Because I love Kaleido Stage.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.890
But of course, I love comedy too.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:13.800
I see.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:16.500
So, your dream is to make the
audience laugh on Kaleido Stage.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.330
Yep.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:21.270
Well, if it's your dream, Sora's already
made it come true, right Sora?

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.240
What's the matter?

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.500
Well...

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:33.700
The stand-up comedian, Jack Barron
will be at the Comedy Theater?

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:35.280
What? What?

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.650
Is he funny?

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.220
I'm not sure.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.160
'Cause I haven't seen him in ten years.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.320
What do you mean "haven't seen him"?

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.690
He's my father.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.090
What?

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.900
No, stop it, Bacchus! Stop it!

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.730
Here, give it back to me!

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:59.270
Ribbit, ribbit!

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:00.740
Wait, Bacchus!

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:03.380
Give Anna's shoe back, ribbit!

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.150
The thing I still remember is
that he used to imitate

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:09.450
frog or owl sounds and made me
and my friends laugh.

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:21.760
Anna, I need to talk to you.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:23.260
Who are you?

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.830
I'm... To tell you the truth,

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.340
I'm an alien from planet Jaga Imo.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:29.440
And my name is "Jaga Imo" jaga.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.770
If you don't hurry up,
you won't have dinner.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.400
We got scolded, jaga.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:36.840
But, then, one day...

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.280
Why, Jack?

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.050
Please understand, Julia.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.020
I don't understand.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.860
If I stay like this, I'll be ruined.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:57.460
Daddy!

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:02.070
Daddy!

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.310
See you later!

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:07.170
Please come back soon!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:12.770
But, after that, he never came back.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:18.490
An talent agent who specialized in
comedians told him that

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:22.120
he could get him cast in a famous TV show.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:25.650
But... He's never been on TV.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.520
Well, you hear this kind of
story all the time.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.860
Since then, have you seen your father?

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.460
No, not even once.

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:35.040
He sends a Christmas card once a while.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:36.970
His address keeps changing,

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:39.640
so there was no way for me contact him.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:40.910
Oh...

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:45.680
That's why you have been checking
performers at the Comedy Theater.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.170
Because you never know when your father
may perform at the Comedy Theater.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.450
Well... That's sorta a reason.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.940
But I truly love comedy.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:58.880
Hey, the Comedy Theater is close by! Right?

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.060
Well, in that case, we have to go!

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:04.100
When I actually have a chance to meet him,

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.030
a part of me wants to, and
another part of me is scared.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:09.070
We shall accompany you, your highness!

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:09.870
What?

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.310
Don't! Don't!

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.800
Didn't you hear what I said?!
Don't put your hand in my back!

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:20.940
What the hell are you doing?!
Take your hand out of my back!

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:22.950
Anna's father...

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:23.950
Hm? Did you say something?

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:23.950
I wonder if he'll notice Anna.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:24.320
I'm hard of hearing nowadays.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:24.320
I wonder if he'll notice Anna.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:24.750
I'm hard of hearing nowadays.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:25.750
I'm hard of hearing nowadays.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:25.750
Since he hasn't seen her for ten years,

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:26.490
The thing getting harder is not your hearing.

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:26.490
Since he hasn't seen her for ten years,

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:27.690
The thing getting harder is not your hearing.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:27.690
I'm sure he'll be surprised.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.950
Isn't it also getting harder to
go back home to your wife?

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.200
Thank you, thank you.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.820
Hey, you thank them too!

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.560
Thank you very much.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.300
Hey, that is my voice!

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:48.240
Next up is a man who missed
taking the world by storm.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.180
Jack Barron!

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:54.180
Everyone, please welcome him with a
warm round of applause.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:05.490
That old man's been using the same old
material for the last 20 years.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:10.230
All that's changed is that he got bald
and the puppet got dentures.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:14.400
And the level of audience went downhill.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:19.040
What's wrong?

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.870
You guys look like you're not having fun.

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:26.940
So you two are dating?

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.180
Yes.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:31.120
The girl you brought here yesterday
was better looking.

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:32.620
What!

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.990
Hey, you, what the hell are you saying?

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.150
He's lying. Lying!

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:37.450
But, don't worry.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:41.020
You're skinnier than the girl
he brought here yesterday.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.360
Oh, wait...

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.360
That's enough!

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.140
Thanks for the beer.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:58.140
Be careful on the way home.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:05.410
Anna...

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.580
Daddy... Daddy...

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:20.670
Look at that.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:23.300
The little mermaid of Kaleido Stage is here.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:24.610
What?

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:27.440
Oh... Hello...

00:08:28.010 --> 00:08:30.850
The girl who plays the little mermaid

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:33.310
Looks more like a blowfish in a fashion show.

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:39.150
The Little Mermaid is without a doubt
a dreamlike story.

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:43.920
Is it a story of a blowfish girl
who is trying to be a princess?

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:47.560
This is... my dad?

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:48.550
This is...?

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.360
Anna, you're cute!

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:59.160
Come on, Anna, your mom is waiting.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:01.770
Daddy...

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:06.780
I expect Kaleido Stage to turn into a
seafood restaurant any day now.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:10.880
Oh, Anna!

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:12.480
Anna, wait a second!

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:20.290
Looks like everyone's in a hurry today.

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:23.460
Is it the basketball finals today?

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:40.210
It seems like there's still a fan of
Jack Barron other than myself out there.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.290
Come to New York with me.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:48.850
Make your family proud!

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:53.260
Daddy... Where are you going?

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:54.520
Daddy...

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:56.820
Daddy!

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.700
He fooled me.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:19.090
It was great.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:20.620
A good job, Anna.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:22.890
I'm glad to see that you're doing fine.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:26.160
Sorry about yesterday, making you feel bad.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:27.830
Don't worry.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:30.130
By the way, what happened
with your father after that?

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:31.900
Well...

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:34.330
I think it's better not to see him anymore.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.030
What! Why?

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:41.470
Jack Barron abandoned my mom and me,
and turned into another man.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:46.480
I don't think he wants to see
his daughter now.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:48.440
Anna...

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:56.420
She still has a long way to go
to be a comedian.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:57.910
Why don't we go there one more time?

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:03.000
Wait!

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:03.860
Sora!

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:19.080
Please wait!

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:21.720
Wait!

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:26.050
Oh... Excuse me!

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.310
Please wait!

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:36.160
What did you do to Sora?!

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.630
Mr. Policeman. It's not what you think.

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:43.940
Is this revenge for yesterday?

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:45.110
No.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:46.630
Because you ran away...

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:49.570
You came to see Anna, didn't you?

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:53.540
I just happened to be in the neighborhood.

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:59.710
Anna told me a story about her father
when she was little.

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:03.280
She told me that he was nice father
who made her laugh a lot.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:07.560
"Even though he's an unpopular comedian
who keeps making the audience mad. "

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:08.630
Isn't that what she said?

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:09.600
She didn't say that...

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:13.060
There's no point for her to meet
with a father like me.

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:16.900
You must be thirsty from all that running.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:18.040
Well...

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:21.510
Excuse me,

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:23.370
how long will you be staying in town?

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:25.580
Until tomorrow.

00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:27.510
Once I finish the evening show,
I'm leaving town.

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:29.880
What! That soon?

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:35.290
Well, anyway, I was invited onstage because
the owner of the theater felt pity for me.

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:39.930
It says, "Once again, a silly person
somewhere around here

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:44.060
is poking her nose into
something she should not. "

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:46.600
Liar.

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:49.130
I remember this card meant
something better than that.

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:52.910
It seems like you've become a little wiser.

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:54.740
This is the reversed position of The Moon.

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:56.580
It means that one will acknowledge his faults,

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:57.980
and remove a misunderstanding.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.180
And he can correct his course and bring
himself into the right direction.

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:01.310
It is a card for hope.

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:02.880
Okay.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:06.320
I will do my best so that Anna and her dad
can meet one more time.

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:12.120
Your father told me that tomorrow
night's show will be the last one.

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:13.630
Oh, no!

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:14.600
What?

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.590
It shrunk...

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:18.570
Hey, Anna,

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:20.630
why don't you go see your father after all?

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:23.070
Well, maybe, I should...

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:23.840
What?

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:25.400
I should have eggs sunny-side-up
for breakfast.

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:29.380
Hey,

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:33.310
your father said he is waiting
at the restaurant near the pier.

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:35.950
Anna...

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:41.560
Sora, her father is the talk of cast.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:42.390
What?!

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:45.360
Don't you think it will be better

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:46.990
to just quietly keep an eye on how
everything turns out once in a while?

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.130
Welcome!

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:57.570
Mr. Barron...

00:13:58.240 --> 00:13:59.770
Oh... Well...

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:03.310
I know you took the time to come here, but...

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:04.580
I already know.

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:06.600
Of course, she doesn't want to see me.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:08.420
Oh no.

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:09.580
It's my fault.

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:15.260
If I hadn't poked my nose into her business,

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:18.920
Anna might have come
to see you on her own.

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:22.200
Anna is lucky,

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:23.390
having a nice friend like you.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:26.830
Well... I don't know if I could say
I'm doing this for Anna.

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:28.320
I...

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:31.370
I lost my parents in a car accident
when I was young.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:32.340
What?!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.800
I thought... Since Anna can
still see her father,

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:42.510
she should meet him and talk about
many things like she used to do.

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:44.920
So...

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:48.080
I'm doing this not for Anna, but for myself.

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:52.220
Sorry... I...

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.660
Oh... What's wrong with me?

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:02.330
Hey, Little Mermaid, snap out of it.

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:05.200
Tears don't suit you.

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:14.080
When Anna cried,

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:16.450
this always cheered her up.

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:21.310
Please bring a large serving of chocolate
chip ice cream to this little mermaid!

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:28.800
Hello.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:30.230
Oh... Mom?

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:32.260
Anna? Are you doing all right?

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:34.570
Yes. How about you?

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:38.270
Just wondering what I should do with
the window that Bacchus just broke.

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:40.570
What's wrong?

00:15:40.570 --> 00:15:41.970
Something happened?

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:43.970
I met Dad.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:45.840
What! Jack?

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:49.950
Yes. At the Comedy Theater in Cape Mary.

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.280
Comedy Theater...

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:52.720
Do you know the place?

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.120
Of course!

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:58.110
I met your dad at that
Comedy Theater a long time ago.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:15:59.290
What?!

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:06.690
One day, an inexperienced new comedian
showed up to meet the owner, Bob.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:11.140
From that evening, Jack appeared on stage
at the Comedy Theater.

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:13.870
He was warmhearted and funny.

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:15.600
And he had an original personal technique.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:19.130
He became very popular
at the theater in no time.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:23.980
Before I knew it,
I was also a big fan of Jack Barron.

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:27.550
But, he's different now.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:31.760
When a guy makes the audience mad
and gets a kick out of it,

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.090
I don't call him a comedian.

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:34.760
That is the worst!

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.000
Did you tell Jack?

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:37.790
What?

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:39.630
How you feel.

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:41.370
If what you said is true,

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:46.140
the only person who can save
the current Jack Barron is you.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.040
Please give my best regards to Jack.

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:57.010
Thank you. Thank you.

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:02.310
Next up is Jack Barron, whose performance
here tonight will be his last.

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:08.180
Do your best, Jack boy.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:11.230
So Anna didn't come after all.

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:12.930
They will have another chance to meet.

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:13.730
Yes.

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:19.240
Huh!

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:20.940
So, the audience is still here.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:25.940
Well, it's true that you can't see this
kind of stupid ventriloquism on TV.

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:28.550
Hm?

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:30.310
You're wearing nice looking glasses.

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:32.710
As a matter of fact, I have some too.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:35.920
Oh, this is the best.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:40.120
When I wear this, I don't need to see
that girl's same old face.

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.560
Hey, what are you saying?!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.260
Oh... This again...

00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:51.760
Look, look, look...

00:17:54.310 --> 00:17:56.340
You're chilling the audience.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:57.470
What the hell are you doing?

00:17:57.950 --> 00:17:59.610
Anna?!

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:00.810
Anna?

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:03.180
This is a surprise.

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:05.720
You and your mom are exactly alike.

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:09.310
Well, of course, your mom was
30% prettier than you.

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:14.360
If you're such a comedian,
why don't you make the audience laugh,

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:15.190
Jack Barron?

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:19.620
Or, are you just a JUNK Baron now?

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:23.740
Junk Baron Jack Barron.

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:26.100
That is a perfect stage name for me.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:31.040
Didn't you say you would
make it big in New York?

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.810
Then what are you doing in this
shabby comedy house?

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.380
Ten years ago...

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.920
The agent who scouted me

00:18:38.920 --> 00:18:41.510
said that he would help me debut
all over the U. S.

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:43.310
He was a very capable man.

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:47.320
Jack Barron abandoned his family
and followed that guy.

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:48.700
Thanks to that agent,

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:52.060
I ended up going around to all of the
comedy theaters in New York every day...

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:54.200
trying to find a job.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:55.100
What?

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:57.470
What happened to that capable agent?

00:18:58.640 --> 00:19:01.010
He was drinking every night...

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:02.000
with my money.

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:03.010
What?

00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:05.810
I was rejected by all the
comedy theaters in New York.

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:09.570
In the end, I was even rejected at a dairy
shop on the state line of New Jersey.

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:14.180
So, it was like the NYC Marathon
out of season.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:19.250
A month passed by, and when I came
back to the cheap New York hotel,

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:23.460
the agent, my money and
my luggage were all gone.

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:26.390
Seems like that he was more
talented in THAT kind of area.

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:30.700
Then, you should have come back home!

00:19:31.010 --> 00:19:32.940
What the hell were you doing for ten years?

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:35.340
I lost my hat.

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:36.880
I kept looking for that hat...

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.450
in back alleys and underpasses.

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:42.010
I also used to search in the trash bins
at the posh hotels.

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:44.890
Ironically,

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:46.890
I realized,

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:51.320
when I finally came back to the
stage after so many years away...

00:19:52.990 --> 00:19:54.360
Daddy!

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:57.690
The one I want to make laugh...

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.660
The one I want to make laugh
one more time is...

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:05.270
Then, why don't you make me laugh
like you used to...

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:06.260
You're a comedian, aren't you?

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:09.710
Make your darling daughter laugh, Jack.

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:14.040
Mr. Jack!

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:25.620
Remember this?

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:32.560
Anna, you're cute.

00:20:39.010 --> 00:20:39.840
Anna...

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:42.980
Please, Anna.

00:20:42.980 --> 00:20:44.510
If you cry with this,

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:47.210
I won't know what to do.

00:20:58.390 --> 00:20:59.690
Anna...

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:06.860
Daddy...

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:22.370
Don't you want to be my partner, Anna?

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:23.550
What?

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:28.150
My current dream is right here, so...

00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:30.560
I see...

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:33.820
Where are you going now?

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:38.820
I'm heading to a comedy theater in
St. Louis that Bob recommended me to.

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:42.740
I'll revive Jack Barron one more time.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:43.930
Then, so long.

00:21:45.270 --> 00:21:46.330
Oh, Daddy!

00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:50.900
Good luck, Daddy.

00:21:51.610 --> 00:21:53.240
Mom said hello.

00:21:53.380 --> 00:21:55.310
Okay. Then, I'm going.

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:08.300
My father is Jack Barron.

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:14.530
The Jack Barron I loved since I was little.

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:24.450
<i>When you're lonely, what do you do?</i>

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:24.450
<i>When you sabishii toki doushitemasuka</i>

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:26.880
<i>Never say you don't get any of that</i>

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:26.880
<i>Never say sonna no wakannai</i>

00:22:26.880 --> 00:22:29.750
<i>Sleep, play, flip through a magazine</i>

00:22:26.880 --> 00:22:29.750
<i>Nemuru asobu magazine mekuru</i>

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:32.090
<i>When you're lonely, you're lonely</i>

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:32.090
<i>Sabishii toki wa sabishii yo</i>

00:22:32.090 --> 00:22:36.860
<i>Like always, invisible vibes fly around
the city today, tulututu</i>

00:22:32.090 --> 00:22:36.860
<i>Mienai denpa ga kyou mo
tulututu machi ni tobikau</i>

00:22:36.860 --> 00:22:41.530
<i>Anyway, the vector of my heart is
talking about so many reasons</i>

00:22:36.860 --> 00:22:41.530
<i>Anyway kokoro no bekutoru
so many reason hanashiteru</i>

00:22:41.530 --> 00:22:46.230
<i>I want to be free and fly the skies</i>

00:22:41.530 --> 00:22:46.230
<i>Jiyuu ni sora o tobitai keredo</i>

00:22:46.230 --> 00:22:50.900
<i>But I don't have space to spread my wings</i>

00:22:46.230 --> 00:22:50.900
<i>Hane o hirogeru basho ga nai</i>

00:22:50.900 --> 00:22:53.070
<i>But I have faith</i>

00:22:50.900 --> 00:22:53.070
<i>Demo shinjiteru</i>

00:22:53.070 --> 00:22:57.780
<i>There is a future yet to be shaped</i>

00:22:53.070 --> 00:22:57.780
<i>Katachi no nai mirai ga aru yo</i>

00:22:57.780 --> 00:23:02.450
<i>And there's a me that I want to shape</i>

00:22:57.780 --> 00:23:02.450
<i>Katachi ni shitai watashi ga iru</i>

00:23:02.450 --> 00:23:08.920
<i>Even if I'm sad, even if it's a mistake</i>

00:23:02.450 --> 00:23:08.920
<i>Kanashikutemo machigai demo</i>

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:14.260
<i>I'll do what I want and
fly towards the freedom</i>

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:14.260
<i>Omou mama fly to the free</i>

00:23:22.640 --> 00:23:25.700
Why am I so concerned about that girl?

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:28.240
And so, once again, another ordeal.

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:29.910
This time is rope walking?!

00:23:29.910 --> 00:23:31.380
Moreover, underneath the rope
is a sea of fire.

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:34.140
This is a big chance, with an opportunity
to co-star with Miss Layla on the line.

00:23:34.210 --> 00:23:37.980
I'll make sure I will do it successfully.
I will. I will!

00:23:38.050 --> 00:23:42.610
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"An Amazingly Hot New Production"

00:23:42.760 --> 00:23:43.420
An Amazingly Hot New Production

00:23:43.420 --> 00:23:45.590
An Amazingly Hot New Production

00:23:43.420 --> 00:23:45.590
My wings are my dream
and on toward the sky...

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.790
An Amazingly Hot New Production
